# ============================================================================
# Frozen StageReceipt / VerificationReceipt contract v1 — contract-freeze gate.
#
# Architecture §21 (execution framework), §21.3 (stage receipt), §21.4
# (fallback rules), §26 (contract freeze, group 7), §6.4 (MappingShardRef).
#
# Like the ID-TAG and MAP gates this proves three separate things, because
# round-tripping alone is not enough for a frozen contract:
#
#   1. EXACT BYTES — encoder output equals a hand-derived golden vector. This
#      is what actually freezes the format; a round-trip test alone passes
#      happily even if encoder and decoder drift together. Wave 0b injected a
#      symmetric field swap that round-tripped perfectly and was caught only
#      here.
#   2. ROUND TRIP — decode(encode(x)) reconstructs x for every record shape.
#   3. REJECTION — malformed, truncated, cross-typed, wrong-version and
#      structurally-inconsistent buffers are refused rather than coerced.
#
# And a fourth thing this group alone has to prove:
#
#   4. NO SILENT FALLBACK — a cost-policy CPU selection and a forced GPU
#      fallback are distinguishable, and a receipt that changed mode without
#      naming a reason cannot be encoded at all. That is the property the
#      whole lane plan rests on, so it is asserted directly and not inferred
#      from the presence of a field.
# ============================================================================

